.TH LINEAR 1 2000-1月 "elastic_model" "elastic_model"
.SH NAME
elastic_model \- Build the in silico perturbation engine from a fitted linear GRN model.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIelastic_model(\fBgrn\fR as <generic> GeneRegulatoryNetwork, 
\fBopts\fR as <generic> ElasticNetPerturbationOptions = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
\fBstrict\fR as boolean = TRUE, 
\fBscale\fR as string = "linear", 
\fBpropagation\fR as string = "cascade", 
\fBsteps\fR as integer = -1, 
\fBdamping\fR as double = -1, 
\fBknockdown_residual\fR as double = -1, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Build the in silico perturbation engine from a fitted linear GRN model.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBgrn\fB \fR\- 
 the fitted [GeneRegulatoryNetwork](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Model.Network.Regulons.LinearRegression.GeneRegulatoryNetwork) object, it is the
 \fBgrn\fR slot of the \fBelastic_net\fR result.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBopts\fB \fR\- the perturbation options, a default configuration is used when this argument is not given. 
.PP
.PP
\fBstrict\fB \fR\- 
 in the strict mode an error will be thrown when the target gene of the perturbation
 is not found in the model; in the non strict mode a warning will be printed and the
 wildtype expression will be returned with the \fBUndefined\fR flag marked as TRUE.
 For a batch run of hundreds of the perturbations it is recommended to disable it and
 to check the \fBMissingGenes\fR field of the result.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBscale\fB \fR\- 
 the numeric space of the expression matrix that was used to fit the network:
 \fBlinear\fR (default) or \fBlog2cpm\fR (i.e. \fBlog2(x + 1)\fR). For a log transformed
 matrix this argument is required, otherwise the knockdown magnitude will be
 over-estimated by about 2~3 times.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBpropagation\fB \fR\- 
 \fBcascade\fR (default) propagates the perturbation to the steady state,
 \fBonehop\fR only keeps the direct effects,
 \fBdelta\fR propagates the change only (recommended for the context conditioned
 prediction: it is numerically identical to "mutant minus the matched control").
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBsteps\fB \fR\- the max cascade iteration steps, a value that is less than 1 means "use the default". 
.PP
.PP
\fBdamping\fB \fR\- the damping factor of the cascade iteration, a value that is less than or equals to 0 means "use the default". 
.PP
.PP
\fBknockdown_residual\fB \fR\- 
 the fraction of the wildtype expression that is kept after a knockdown,
 a negative value means "use the default" (0.2, i.e. about 80% knockdown).
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment object. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
an [ElasticNet](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.CellPhenotype.ElasticNet) engine which implements the
 [InsilicoPerturbationExperiment](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.BNLearn.InsilicoPerturbationExperiment) interface.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
linear
